#: ../../../policy/CMP0221.rst:2
msgid "CMP0221"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../policy/CMP0221.rst:6
msgid ""
":command:`cmake_host_system_information` ``DISTRIB_*`` queries read the host "
"os-release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../policy/CMP0221.rst:9
msgid ""
"The :command:`cmake_host_system_information` command is documented to query "
"information about the host system on which CMake runs.  However, its "
"``DISTRIB_*`` queries read the :file:`/etc/os-release` (or :file:`/usr/lib/"
"os-release`) file under the :variable:`CMAKE_SYSROOT`, if set. During cross "
"compilation this reports the *target* distribution rather than the host, "
"contradicting the rest of the command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../policy/CMP0221.rst:16
msgid ""
"The ``OLD`` behavior of this policy is for ``DISTRIB_*`` queries with no "
"``FROM_SYSROOT`` to read the os-release under :variable:`CMAKE_SYSROOT`. The "
"``NEW`` behavior is for such queries to read the host os-release, ignoring :"
"variable:`CMAKE_SYSROOT`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../policy/CMP0221.rst:21
msgid ""
"Either behavior may be requested explicitly, regardless of this policy, with "
"the ``FROM_SYSROOT <bool>`` option:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../policy/CMP0221.rst:24
msgid "A false value reads the host os-release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../policy/CMP0221.rst:25
msgid ""
"A true value reads the os-release under :variable:`CMAKE_SYSROOT`, which is "
"useful for querying the target distribution (e.g. for packaging)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../policy/CMP0221.rst:28
msgid ""
"# Always the host distribution:\n"
"cmake_host_system_information(RESULT host QUERY FROM_SYSROOT OFF "
"DISTRIB_ID)\n"
"\n"
"# Always the target (CMAKE_SYSROOT) distribution:\n"
"cmake_host_system_information(RESULT target QUERY FROM_SYSROOT ON DISTRIB_ID)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../policy/CMP0221.rst:36
msgid ""
"The warning is issued only when it can matter: a ``DISTRIB_*`` query with no "
"``FROM_SYSROOT`` while :variable:`CMAKE_SYSROOT` is non-empty.  Passing "
"``FROM_SYSROOT``, or leaving :variable:`CMAKE_SYSROOT` empty, is silent."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../policy/include/STANDARD_ADVICE.rst:1
msgid ""
"This policy was introduced in CMake version |INTRODUCED_IN_CMAKE_VERSION|. "
"It may be set by :command:`cmake_policy` or :command:"
"`cmake_minimum_required`. If it is not set, CMake |WARNS_OR_DOES_NOT_WARN|, "
"and uses ``OLD`` behavior."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../policy/include/DEPRECATED.rst:2
msgid ""
"The ``OLD`` behavior of a policy is :ref:`deprecated by definition <cmake-"
"policies-intro>` and may be removed in a future version of CMake."
msgstr ""
